vendor/ -- third-party material we did not write and do not maintain.

Held unmodified.  A drop that needs changing to build is changed by a patch
in src/ or a step in tools/, never by an edit here.

Licensing: ../LICENSE covers work written for this project, not this
material.  The Digital Research dev-pack files below were shared with the
CP/M-8000 release and its source.

  z8001mb/    vendor/z8001mb/cpm8k/packages/base/, taken from 4sun5bu's
              Z8001MB project, <https://github.com/4sun5bu/Z8001MB>, master
              as of 2026-07-30.  Holds Digital Research's CP/M-8000 dev-pack
              binaries and headers (zcc/zcc1/zcc2/zcc3, asz8k + asz8k.pd,
              ld8k, ar8k, ddt, ed, pip, stat, dump, nmz8k, sizez8k, xcon,
              xdump, libcpm.a, startup.o/startup.8kn, and the *.h headers) --
              every file present is staged by name onto drive A: by
              tools/stage-devpack.sh.  Nothing else from the upstream drop is
              kept here: only what the build actually reads.

The CP/M 3 and CP/M-8000 reference sources this port was derived from
(Digital Research's 8080 CP/M 3, the May 1983 and October 1983 CP/M-8000
snapshots, and CP/M-8000 v1.3 for the Olivetti M20) are reference material,
not build inputs. 
